DESCRIPTION:November 24 marks Carménère Day\, which commemorates a case o
 f mistaken identity. For more than a century Chilean growers tended a Bord
 eaux grape they believed was Merlot\; in 1994 a French ampelographer looke
 d at the vines and said they were Carménère\, a variety phylloxera and p
 oor fruit set had all but erased in France. The trade body Wines of Chile 
 launched the day in 2014\, on the twentieth anniversary of that correction
 .\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/national-carmenere-day/
